  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "This categorical finite-presentation descent theorem must descend entire scheme objects, all morphisms and equality relations across arbitrary affine-transition inverse systems. Its proof constructs finite affine models, synchronizes overlap opens and isomorphisms at successive indices, and enforces the cocycle before gluing, without a Noetherian or separatedness assumption. The global categorical coherence construction is beyond routine ring coefficient descent.",
